      //   q8   |  15.70   |  22.08              |  28
      //   q4   |   9.15   |  15.53              |  20
      //
      // `qwen_image_2_1_turbo_every_floor_key_the_ui_reads_has_a_worker_source` pins these to the
      // linked accessor on macOS. No `calibrations`, no measured row on either lane; Turbo's
      // calibration fingerprints (`TURBO_MEMORY_CALIBRATION_FINGERPRINT`, a different value on
      // each lane) key the hand-authored request-owned contracts below, so a record built for one
      // id can never satisfy the other's handshake. The terminal campaign owns the anchors.
      "mlx": {

        // Base's default-tier declaration (an app-wide q8 default; no `minQualityTier`).
        "quantize": 8
      },
      // The off-Mac lane. Candle holds the bf16 Turbo VAE at its compute width exactly as it holds
      // base's f32 VAE (`memory_strategy::compute_width()`), so Turbo's DERIVED Candle floors are
      // base's arithmetic over the same inputs — resident + the 3-map untiled decode tail at
      // 2400x1792, x1.25 — and land on the same integers. They are stated here as Turbo's own
      // derivation, not copied as evidence: `binding` for `vram_gate::predicted_peak_gb`, the
      // scalar the densest tier's floor, and no measured key.
      //   bf16 45 — 28.61 + 6.92 = 35.53 GiB x1.25 = 44.41
      //   q8   30 — 16.33 + 6.92 = 23.25 GiB x1.25 = 29.07
      //   q4   21 —  9.78 + 6.92 = 16.70 GiB x1.25 = 20.88
      "candle": {

      },
      "ui": {
        "label": "Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo",
        "description": "Qwen-Image 2.1 Turbo — the distilled, few-step sibling of Qwen Image 2.1, ported natively to MLX on Apple Silicon and Candle on NVIDIA CUDA (Windows/Linux). The same ~7.1B single-stream flow-matching transformer over a 64-channel latent with a ~7.6B Qwen3-VL language tower, distilled to render in 8 steps over the schedule saved with the weights; other step counts resample that saved curve, and picking a scheduler other than Default replaces it with that scheduler's own curve. It keeps everything the base model offers — seven aspect presets up to 2752 px, 1-10 ordered reference images for editing, transparent (RGBA) output, Qwen Image 2.1 LoRAs — with true classifier-free guidance off by default. Distributed under the Qwen RESEARCH LICENSE AGREEMENT: research and evaluation use only, with a separate commercial licence required from Alibaba. Three precision tiers — bf16, Q8 and Q4: bf16 runs on both backends, and the Q8 and Q4 tiers are verified on Apple Silicon (MLX); they have not yet been run on an NVIDIA card. The bf16 tier is downloaded from Qwen's own repository on first use; the Q8 and Q4 tiers are quantized derivatives re-hosted by SceneWorks, each carrying the licence, the attribution notice and a CHANGES.md record of what was changed.",
        "recommendedFor": ["text_to_image", "edit_image"],
        // Base's multi-reference editor surface; the picker's ceiling is `limits.maxReferenceAssets`.
        "multiReference": true,
        // Turbo's own guide (sc-25908): base's prompt format and ordered-reference conventions,
