      // TASK IDENTITY (E4). The upstream repo ships THREE task backbones side by side — generation
      // at the root, `depth/` and `upscaler/` — and only generation conditions on text. This entry
      // is the generation task alone: its primary download fetches exactly the root `config.yaml` +
      // `model.safetensors` (never `depth/*` / `upscaler/*`), and the Qwen3-VL encoder is a
      // SEPARATE `coRequisite` component tagged `componentId: "text_encoder"`, so the depth and
      // restoration tasks can be their own catalog entries that install and run without it.
      // The worker stages that component as `LoadSpec::components["text_encoder"]`
      // (gen_core::iris::TEXT_ENCODER_COMPONENT) from the pinned snapshot; it never downloads at
      // generation time.
      //
      // CONTROL SURFACE (E3) — exactly what the engine honours (sc-25681): prompt, negative prompt
      // (the CFG unconditional), size on a 16-px grid (16..=2048), count <= 8, seed, steps,
      // guidance (= upstream cfg_scale), the FlowDPM-Solver++ order as a sampler (`dpmpp_2m` =
      // order 2, the default; `euler` = order 1), the schedule shift (upstream `shift`, default
      // the checkpoint's flow.shift = 4.0; there is one shifted time grid, so no scheduler menu),
      // the CFG interval, the caption-overflow policy, and generation-task LoRA/LoKr adapters
      // stamped family=iris + irisTask=generation. Prediction target / train timesteps come from
      // the checkpoint (no knob).
      //
      // TIERS (sc-26266). Both native engines quantize the backbone and Qwen3-VL text
      // encoder at LOAD TIME from the same dense upstream files; no converted weights are
      // downloaded or redistributed. Embeddings and norms remain dense. All three rows share
      // one complete snapshot. `advanced.mlxQuantize` 0 / 8 / 4 selects bf16 / q8 / q4 on
      // either backend; `mlx.quantize: 0` preserves bf16 when no tier is selected.
      // A negative prompt or a CFG interval only exists under CFG: at guidance 1.0 the engine
      // refuses either, so the API refuses them and Image Studio disables both controls there.
      "id": "iris_3b",
      "name": "Iris 3B",
      "family": "iris",
      "type": "image",
      "adapter": "mlx_iris",
      // Served on both lanes: `mlx-gen-iris` on Apple Silicon (sc-25679) and `candle-gen-iris` on
