      "candle": {
        // DECLARED floor, the Candle twin of the MLX value above. `measured: false` is this row's
        // evidence class for a MEASURED `vramGbByTier` ladder, which Supra2 does not carry; the
        // measured evidence lives in the anchor store instead: the sc-24217 campaign measured
        // envelope `imc-720c45380d2ce4058aa0` (config/memory-anchors.json `analyticOnly`;
        // docs/calibration/sc-24217/supra2-img-bf16-candle-evidence.json) is 2.82 GB of VRAM, flat
        // from count 1 to count 8 because the VAE decodes the batch's images one at a time. The
        // 4 GB floor stays above that measurement. `candle-gen-supra2` is resident-only (no quantization, sequential
        // offload or deferred materialization): every tensor is read once and lives on the device
        // for the generator's lifetime. The resident f32 set is ~1.2 GB (the 416 MB denoiser, the
        // Flan-T5-Base encoder half of the 990 MB checkpoint, the 335 MB VAE) plus 256x256
        // activations (a 32x32 latent = 256 tokens; the decoder at 256x256). Like every padded
