      // DECLARED (measured: false) admission for the depth job (`depth_jobs::DepthAdmission`); the
      // epic-end campaign (sc-25684) replaces it with measured evidence. Existing real-weight
      // evidence: a 1024x2048 photo at the default 1024 cap (model input 512x1024 = 524288 px) peaked
      // at 9.4 GB on MLX and 8.4 GB (nvidia-smi) on CUDA. `residentGb` is the bf16 backbone + reducer
      // (~3B parameters) the forward keeps resident; the rest of the reference peak is treated as
      // activations that grow with the model input's pixel count (both engines run fused/budgeted
      // attention, so the transient is linear in tokens), padded by `extrapolationFactor` above the
      // observed area. A request over the host budget is refused before load — never downscaled.
      // The Candle `residentGb` is the card's own reading with the model loaded and nothing running
      // (7306 MiB = 7.13 GiB over the idle baseline, sc-25690 catalog rehearsal run 38403658578):
      // the gate compares against device-level free VRAM, which also counts the CUDA context, so
      // the backbone's tensor bytes alone (6.5) under-stated an input smaller than the reference.
      // The measured facts (`measured` and each lane's `residentGb` / `referencePeakGb`) live in
      // config/manifests/registry/evidence.json under `depth.admission` and are projected here;
      // the reference geometry and extrapolation factor are declared parameters (SW-7032).
      "depth": {
        "admission": {
          "referenceModelPixels": 524288,
          "extrapolationFactor": 1.5
        }
      },
      "mlx": {
        // Catalog display floor (unified memory) for the default 1024 cap; the job's own admission
        // above is what gates a request.

      },
      "candle": {
        // 8.4 GB recorded peak at the reference geometry + the 2 GB allocator reserve, rounded up.

      },
