        "description": "Black Forest Labs FLUX.2 [klein] 9B — 4-step distilled text-to-image + reference editing, running natively through MLX on Apple Silicon and Candle/CUDA on Windows/Linux. 9B flow transformer + 8B Qwen3 text embedder; ~36 GB bf16 peak at 1024². Pre-quantized and hosted by SceneWorks (Q4 default ~22 GB; Q8 and bf16 selectable) — downloads ready-to-run with no install-time conversion. Only the transformer is quantized; the Qwen3 text encoder stays full-precision bf16 in every tier for fidelity. Distributed under the FLUX Non-Commercial License (non-commercial use only); SceneWorks hosts a public, ungated re-host, so no Hugging Face token or license acceptance is needed before downloading. For faster reference editing on the same architecture, see FLUX.2 [klein] 9B-KV.",
