        "description": "NVIDIA SANA-Sprint 1.6B — the few-step SANA distillation, ported natively to MLX on Apple Silicon and Candle on NVIDIA CUDA (Windows/Linux). The same 1.6B linear-attention transformer, 32× DC-AE, and Gemma 2 instruction text encoder as base SANA support text-to-image plus reference-guided image-to-image. Its CFG-free SCM/TrigFlow sampler and guidance-embedding trunk generate a 1024×1024 image in about two steps with no negative prompt. Apple Silicon offers pre-packed q4 (default), q8, and bf16 tiers; Candle uses the original dense snapshot. The SANA transformer and VAE are licensed by NVIDIA under Apache-2.0; the bundled Gemma 2 text encoder is governed by Google's Gemma Terms of Use and Prohibited Use Policy.",
        "recommendedFor": ["text_to_image", "image_to_image"],
