          "footprint": { "diskSizeBytes": 5690000000 }
        }
      ],
      "defaults": {
        // diffusers FlowMatchEuler with static time-shift 3.0 (the orthogonal schedulerShift knob, epic
        // 7114), 30 steps, true CFG 4.5. Default solver is the recommended ER-SDE-3 (`er_sde`, sc-10519).
        "resolution": "1024x1024",
        "steps": 30,
        "guidanceScale": 4.5,
        "count": 1,
        "sampler": "er_sde",
        "scheduler": "default",
        "schedulerShift": 3.0
      },
      "limits": {
        // Cosmos RoPE trained window → W×H in [512, 1536], multiples of 16 (descriptor RES_MULTIPLE=16;
        // >1536/side is rejected, not clamped). Anima routes the per-generation sampler/scheduler knobs
        // through the unified flow framework (epic 7114), so the `anima_base` descriptor advertises
        // curated_sampler_names()/curated_scheduler_names() — this `limits` menu is a subset (the
        // engines.rs `manifest_menu_is_subset_of_descriptor` drift guard). "default" is the native loop.
        "resolutions": ["1024x1024", "832x1216", "1216x832", "896x1152", "1152x896", "768x1344", "1344x768", "1536x1536"],
        "count": [1, 2, 4],
        "samplers": ["default", "er_sde", "euler", "euler_ancestral", "heun", "dpmpp_2m", "dpmpp_2m_sde", "dpmpp_sde", "uni_pc", "lcm", "ddim"],
        "schedulers": ["default", "normal", "simple", "karras", "exponential", "sgm_uniform", "beta", "ddim_uniform", "beta57"]
      },
      "loraCompatibility": {
        // Anima LoRA/LoKr (sc-10521): the trained adapter targets the Cosmos DiT AND the bundled
        // `llm_adapter` conditioner, applied via `apply_anima_adapters`. Quant + LoRA TOGETHER is
        // unsupported (sc-10578 — the engine `load()` errors on the combination).
        "families": ["anima"],
        "types": ["style", "character"]
      },
      "mlx": {
        // 2B Cosmos DiT + 0.6B Qwen3 TE + Qwen-Image VAE — small. Convert-at-install packs the DiT to the
        // q4/q8/bf16 matrix on-device (the offline 2B quantize peaks a few GB); default q4. minMemoryGb 16
        // covers both the convert peak and a 1536² generate.

        "quantize": 4,
        // Per-model quality FLOOR (sc-10731, epic 10721): the minimum-fidelity tier the DEFAULT resolution
        // may land on. Anima base renders WASHED/smudged at q4 under CFG 4.5 × 30 steps (sc-10714 — q4
        // weight-quant error is amplified), so the app-wide default (and a low global "default quality"
        // setting) clamps UP to q8 here rather than silently landing on q4. This REPLACES the sc-10714
        // `anima_tier_subdir` q8 hardcode: the q8 default is now floor-driven, not a resolver special-case.
        // An EXPLICIT q4 pick in the Studio picker is still honored (a quant tier is a creative choice) —
        // the web surfaces a non-blocking advisory instead. Turbo omits this floor (it is CFG-free, so q4
        // is acceptable there).
        "minQualityTier": "q8",
        "requiresConversion": true,
        "converter": "anima_quant",
        "convertSourceRepo": "circlestone-labs/Anima",
        // epic-10285 staleness: the converted artifact is stale (needs re-convert) once THIS source file
        // is no longer in the HF cache. Must be one of `ANIMA_DIT_FILES` (validated by the convert plan).
        "convertSourceFile": "split_files/diffusion_models/anima-base-v1.0.safetensors"
      },
      // sc-20799 gap 1: the Candle/CUDA Anima memory ladder, which had no registry rule, no manifest
      // declaration and an all-Missing matrix column. Declaration-driven only — `anima_base` /
      // `anima_aesthetic` / `anima_turbo` are generic `is_candle_engine` txt2img ids, so
      // `image_jobs/base.rs` ALREADY hands them to
      // `candle_memory_strategy::evaluate_shared_image`; these rows are the declaration that call was
      // missing. No worker code change is required or made.
      //
      // Engine truth at the pinned inference rev ebcdc7da79612d19dfe1dbc748c55a9ffe8336e6,
      // crates/media/candle-gen/candle-gen-anima/src/memory_strategy.rs:
      //  - One `contract()` builder serves all three ids (`IDS`), but each gets its OWN calibration
      //    identity `anima-candle-request-scoped-conditioning-v1-<id with '_' -> '-'>`, precisely so a
      //    base calibration can never admit aesthetic/turbo just because their component layout
      //    happens to match. That is why the three entries carry three different fingerprints.
      //  - Resident: Implemented. StagedResidency: Implemented — Qwen3 + the bundled conditioner
      //    produce immutable conditioning, are synchronized and dropped, then the DiT + VAE load
      //    (`MemoryLifecycleCapabilities { synchronized_phase_release: true, .. }`).
      //  - bounded_decode / bounded_attention / bounded_transformer_residency are NOT implemented:
      //    the same lifecycle sets `decode_tiling`, `attention_chunking` and
      //    `transformer_window_materialization` all false, and the crate's own
      //    `all_three_exact_plain_routes_publish_only_staged_residency` test asserts none of those
      //    three rungs ever reads Implemented. They are therefore ABSENT here rather than declared —
      //    the Candle Anima ladder genuinely stops at staged residency.
      //  - Route gate (`loaded_safety_check`): exactly single-phase text_to_image, reference_count 0,
      //    no reference, no PiD, no phases. That is also this entry's entire `capabilities` list, so
      //    the modes/referenceCounts below are the engine-and-catalog INTERSECTION, not a narrowing.
      //  - Tier: `resolved_numeric_tier` refuses any precision but bf16 ("Candle/CUDA memory
      //    residency supports only the native bf16 precision"). Off-Mac there is also no other tier
      //    to select at all — the windows/linux `downloads` row pulls the raw dense `split_files/`
      //    tree and the `anima_quant` converter that packs q4/q8/bf16 is macOS-only. So bf16 is the
      //    only reachable Candle tier, which is why this block's `tiers` is narrower than the mlx
      //    contract's ["bf16","q4","q8"] above.
      "candle": {
        // Staged residency IS the sequential-offload lever on this family: the conditioning phase is
        // released and synchronized before the DiT phase allocates.

      },
      "licenseUrl": "https://huggingface.co/circlestone-labs/Anima",
      "ui": {
        "label": "Anima 2B",
        "description": "CircleStone Labs Anima 2B — an anime text-to-image model running natively through MLX on Apple Silicon and Candle/CUDA on Windows/Linux. A Cosmos-Predict2 diffusion transformer conditioned by a compact query-token text adapter over a Qwen3-0.6B encoder, decoded through the Qwen-Image VAE. Runs ~30 steps at guidance 4.5 (flow-match, ER-SDE-3 sampler, shift 3.0). Uses the danbooru/booru tag convention — comma-separated lowercase tags, spaces not underscores, artists prefixed with `@`; strong prompt weighting works (e.g. `(chibi:2)`), applied to the text query tokens. Convert-at-install on Mac: the ~5.6 GB source is packed on-device into bf16 / q8 (default) / q4 tiers — q8 is the default (near-lossless, ≈bf16); pick bf16 for max fidelity (and, on this small 2B model, often the fastest on Apple Silicon), or q4 for a softer, more painterly look (and to save RAM). Distributed under the CircleStone Labs Non-Commercial License v1.2: generations are for non-commercial use only. Runs comfortably on a 16 GB-class Mac; the Candle lane uses the dense checkpoint off-Mac.",
        "recommendedFor": ["text_to_image"],
        // Booru quality prefix + negative (sc-10523, sc-10760). Image Studio seeds `defaultPrompt` into an
        // UNEDITED prompt box and `defaultNegativePrompt` into an EMPTY negative box (text-to-image AND
        // character mode). Anima is a danbooru-tag model that renders low-effort art from a bare sentence, so
        // opening the prompt with the quality prefix and building on it is what the model card recommends.
        // `promptHint` shows the inline booru tip under the prompt box (and opens the prompt guide).
        "defaultPrompt": "masterpiece, best quality, ",
        "defaultNegativePrompt": "worst quality, low quality, score_1, score_2, score_3, artist name, blurry, jpeg artifacts, chromatic aberration",
        "promptHint": "Booru-tag model: keep the quality prefix and describe your subject as comma-separated tags (e.g. 1girl, solo, pink hair, superhero costume, cape, dynamic pose). A plain sentence renders low-effort art.",
        "promptGuide": {
          "title": "Anima Prompt Guide",
