      // I2V-A14B descriptor declares `conditioning: vec![ConditioningKind::Reference]` with no
      // `Keyframe` (mlx-gen-wan/src/model.rs, pinned by its own registration test), and the candle
      // I2V-A14B descriptor is the same single `Reference` — so gen-core's default-deny
      // `validate_request` makes a keyframe a hard `Unsupported` on BOTH lanes. The 5B (`wan_2_2`)
      // serves FLF because TI2V is a mask-blend/replace-latent architecture whose pinned-frame set
      // is just a list of latent indices; the A14B is channel-concat (`in_dim` 36 = noise 16 +
      // mask 4 + z_video 16) whose mask is hard-pinned to latent frame 0 and whose patch_embedding
      // was trained on "frame 0 image, rest zeros" — a second pinned frame is out-of-distribution
      // for the checkpoint, not a flag flip. Upstream ships no Wan2.2 FLF2V variant of this family
