      "id": "real_esrgan",
      "recommended": true,
      "name": "Real-ESRGAN Upscaler",
      "family": "real-esrgan",
      "type": "utility",
      "adapter": "real-esrgan",
      "capabilities": [],
      "downloads": [
        {
          // The ONNX exports the Rust upscaler ACTUALLY loads (sc-17633). This entry used to
          // declare the upstream `RealESRGAN_x{2,4}plus.pth` pair from `nateraw/real-esrgan`
          // (~134 MB) — weights no lane has read since the Python upscaler was retired. The
          // ONNX the macOS/Windows Rust lane does load was side-loaded at JOB time into
          // `<data_dir>/cache/upscale/` instead, where the Models screen cannot see, size or
          // delete it (6.9 GiB observed). Declaring the real artifacts here makes the install
          // match the load: one Model Manager install, into the HF cache, no mid-render fetch.
          //
          // The loader half landed with it — `upscale_jobs::resolve_onnx` is cache-only and reads
          // this snapshot. Declaring the ONNX WITHOUT that change would have been worse than
          // leaving it alone: install state keys on the declared repo, so the entry would have
          // flipped to "not installed", prompted a 134 MB download the loader ignored, and then
          // still fetched the same bytes mid-upscale.
          //
          // Migration: an existing install keeps working from the legacy `cache/upscale/` copy, so
          // nothing re-downloads. Its old `nateraw/real-esrgan` `.pth` bytes are now orphaned in
          // the HF cache — never loaded, and no longer reachable from this entry's artifact paths.
          // Reclaiming them is tracked on sc-17636 (S11), which owns delete/size coverage.
          //
          // `resources.imageUpscalers.real-esrgan.x{2,4}` still records the `.pth` provenance —
          // Restore `scripts/spikes/sc3489_export_reference.py` from
          // docs/archive/historical-artifacts.md to reproduce these ONNX files from it —
          // but provenance is metadata, not something every user needs on disk.
          //
          // The revision is byte-for-byte the worker's own `ONNX_REVISION`
          // (`upscale_jobs.rs`, sc-9682). They MUST agree: a manifest that installed one
          // revision while the loader resolved another would recreate, at the revision level,
          // exactly the declared-vs-loaded drift this story exists to remove.
          "provider": "huggingface",
          "repo": "SceneWorks/real-esrgan-onnx",
          "revision": "09f741bac80a246b407da3ee902bf5f3291b602f",
          "files": ["real_esrgan_x2.onnx", "real_esrgan_x4.onnx"],
          "estimatedSizeBytes": 134125050
