    {
      // sc-17632 (epic 17625) — the OTHER upscaler, and the same story as SAM3 below: SeedVR2 had
      // no install-flow representation at all. Its repo and pinned revision lived only as
      // hardcoded constants in worker source, DUPLICATED across the two lanes that load it — the
      // `image_upscale` job (`upscale_jobs.rs`) and the `video_upscale` job
      // (`video_jobs/seedvr2.rs`) — and each lane downloaded the SAME ~7.3 GB checkpoint mid-render
      // into its OWN destination (`<data_dir>/cache/upscale/seedvr2/` and
      // `<data_dir>/cache/seedvr2-mlx/`), where the Models screen can neither size nor delete it.
      //
      // The loader half landed with this entry: both lanes now call ONE cache-only resolver,
      // `upscale_jobs::require_seedvr2_checkpoint_dir`. Declaring the repo WITHOUT that change
      // would have been worse than leaving it alone — install state keys on the declared repo, so
      // the entry would have flipped every existing install to "not installed", prompted a 7.3 GB
      // download the loaders ignored, and then still fetched the same bytes inside the next render.
      //
      // Migration: an existing install keeps working from EITHER legacy root, so nothing
      // re-downloads. Those bytes are now orphaned — never written to again, and not reachable from
      // this entry's artifact paths. Reclaiming them is tracked on sc-17636 (S11), which owns
      // delete/size coverage.
      //
      // The revision is byte-for-byte the worker's own `SEEDVR2_REVISION` (`upscale_jobs.rs`,
      // sc-8879), and the files are the upstream names verbatim — the engine loads them unrenamed,
      // straight out of the HF snapshot dir. They MUST agree: `SEEDVR2_REVISION` is a 40-hex pin,
      // so the resolver reads that EXACT `snapshots/<sha>/` with no fall-through to `refs/main`,
      // and a manifest installing a different one would report "installed" while every SeedVR2 job
      // failed with "not installed". `manifest_declares_the_same_seedvr2_pin_the_loader_reads`
      // (upscale_jobs/tests.rs) fails if either side drifts.
      "id": "seedvr2_upscaler",
      "name": "SeedVR2 Upscaler",
      "family": "seedvr2",
      "type": "utility",
      "capabilities": [],
      "downloads": [
        {
          // Third-party mirror of ByteDance-Seed's SeedVR2-3B (Apache-2.0), in the raw ComfyUI
          // layout both engines convert in-memory at load. `numz/SeedVR2_comfyUI` also hosts 7B and
          // fp8 variants this build does not load, so the file allow-list is what keeps the install
          // to the 3B fp16 pair (~7.3 GB) rather than the whole repo.
          "provider": "huggingface",
          "repo": "numz/SeedVR2_comfyUI",
          "revision": "09ced71023636e9bc8cdf9cdecfb2625d1e691e8",
          "files": ["seedvr2_ema_3b_fp16.safetensors", "ema_vae_fp16.safetensors"],
          "estimatedSizeBytes": 7284343622
        }
      ],
      "paths": {
        "model": "${HF_CACHE}/numz/SeedVR2_comfyUI"
      },
      "defaults": {},
      "limits": {},
      "loraCompatibility": {
        "families": [],
        "types": []
      },
      "ui": {
        "label": "SeedVR2 Upscaler",
        // No `promptGuide`: `type: "utility"` entries are exempt (`promptGuideRequiredForModel`)
        // because they never reach a Studio prompt-guide surface, and the three utilities sc-17627
        // declared carry none either. Pointing this at Real-ESRGAN's guide would satisfy the gate
        // while describing a different upscaler. Provenance lives on the About→Licenses `seedvr2`
        // component instead.
        "description": "One-step diffusion super-resolution behind the SeedVR2 image-upscale engine and video upscaling. Larger and slower than Real-ESRGAN, and generative rather than pixel-faithful; install it only if you want that engine.",
        "recommendedFor": ["image_upscale", "video_upscale"]
      }
    },
    {
      // Iris-3B RESTORATION (epic sc-25678, story sc-25683) — the `upscaler/` task of
      // speridlabs/iris-3b, served as the `iris` engine of the image-upscale surfaces (Image Studio
      // post-processing, Image Editor + Library restore actions) by the `iris_3b_restore` transform
      // that BOTH native bundles register (`mlx-gen-iris` on Apple Silicon, `candle-gen-iris` on
      // Windows/Linux NVIDIA).
      //
      // TASK IDENTITY (E4). Its own resource closure: EXACTLY the three files of the `upscaler/`
      // export — the restoration backbone, its `config.yaml` (whose `task: restoration` section the
      // engine checks) and the shipped `empty_prompt.safetensors` conditioning. No text encoder, no
      // generation backbone (the root `config.yaml` / `model.safetensors` belong to `iris_3b`), and
      // no `depth/` files: install state is per-file, so installing the generation model never marks
      // restoration installed or vice versa. The worker resolves the folder cache-only at this
      // revision (`iris_restore::resolve_restore_export_dir`, pinned to the same repo/revision by
      // `manifest_declares_the_restore_closure_the_resolver_reads`); a missing / torn / wrong-task
      // export is a typed refusal before anything loads, and nothing downloads at restore time.
      //
      // MEMORY. DECLARED conservative floors (`measured: false`, no calibration campaign — S6 /
      // sc-25684 owns measured values) from the existing real-weight evidence for a 512x384 →
      // 2048x1536 restore (6 tiles): MLX peak 11.7 GB, CUDA nvidia-smi peak 10.1 GB, rounded up ~20 %
      // to 14 / 12 GB, plus each gate's 2 GB reserve (16 / 14). Tiles are a fixed 1024 px, so the
      // model working set is per-tile bounded; on unified memory the worker adds the host output
