      // Qwen-Image 2.1 OFFICIAL PROMPT REWRITER — text-to-image half (sc-24113, epic 24107).
      //
      // Upstream ships prompt rewriting as a SEPARATE pair of checkpoints, not as anything inside
      // the image model: `Qwen/Qwen-Image-2.1-PE-T2I` rewrites a text-to-image brief, and its
      // sibling `-PE-I2I` (the next entry) rewrites an EDIT instruction against the reference
      // images. Which one applies is decided by the REQUEST — references present means edit — and
      // never by a user-facing model picker.
      //
      // Both are fine-tuned Qwen3.5/3.6 (`model_type` `qwen3_5`) 9.41B VLM checkpoints, which is
      // the SAME architecture the optional `film_planner_qwen3_6_27b` entry above already runs:
      // they load on the existing native TextLlm lane (`adapter: "prompt-refine"` →
      // `mlx-llama` on macOS / `candle-llama` off-Mac, through `Architecture::Qwen35` →
      // `Qwen35Config`/`Qwen35Model`, with `Qwen35VisionModel` + DeepStack serving the I2I image
      // turns). NOTHING new is built to run them; the worker's `prompt_refine` job takes a
      // `qwen_image_rewrite` task and a `payload.model` override, exactly as the film planner does.
