    {
      // Qwen3.8 27B describer (SW-F365, SW-7119): the larger describing model of the dataset
      // batch describe job (`dataset_batch_describe`), selected by its repository as the job's
      // `model`. `huihui-ai/Huihui-Qwen3.8-27B-abliterated` is an abliterated Qwen3.8-27B
      // (`model_type: qwen3_5`, vision encoder kept, apache-2.0, not gated; verified against the
      // Hugging Face API on 2026-11-13 at the pinned revision). It runs on the same native TextLlm
      // path as the Vision Captioner: JSON-constrained decode, thinking off.
      //
      // TIERS. q4 (the default) and q8 are quantised ahead of time with mlx-llm's
      // `prepare_snapshot` (inference 4a36a7f8) and served from the SceneWorks re-host
      // `SceneWorks/qwen3.8-27b-abliterated-mlx` @ 76f3c445 as self-contained `q4/` and `q8/`
      // folders (vision tower kept bf16). bf16 is the upstream repository (18 shards, 55.6 GB).
      // Load-time quantisation is deliberately not offered: MLX load admission prices it at twice
      // the bf16 source, and a q4 user must not download the 55.6 GB. A describe job names its
      // tier as the request's `variant`, so source admission selects the row the worker loads.
      //
      // The re-host rows are `macos`-only because they are MLX snapshots. Candle's quantised
      // snapshot is a different format and its rows are added when that re-host is published;
      // until then a Windows/Linux worker has the bf16 row only.
