    {
      // YuE lyrics2song (epic sc-19373, sc-19383) — six stage-1 checkpoints (en / zh / jp-kr ×
      // CoT / ICL), each its own registered candle-audio-yue provider (`yue_{en,zh,jp_kr}_{cot,icl}`).
      // One render runs stage 1 (7B Llama, this entry's primary) → stage 2 (1B Llama) → xcodec →
      // the vocal + instrumental Vocos upsamplers → a low-band splice, and returns a 44.1 kHz mix plus
      // `vocals` and `instrumental` stems. Candle-only (epic R3 — no MLX audio backend exists).
      //
      // TIERS (epic R2): the stage-1 and stage-2 LMs ship bf16 / q8 / q4 as PHYSICAL pre-quantized
      // subtrees (`<tier>/`, candle-llm `prepare_snapshot`), so a user downloads only the tier they
      // pick — q4 by default. Each tier row carries the stage-2 LM at the SAME tier as a per-tier
      // `coRequisite` (componentId `stage2`, `subdir` = the tier dir), exactly the Mage-Flow sc-14980
      // shape, so `resolve_co_requisites_for_tier` can never pair a q4 stage 1 with a bf16 stage 2.
      //
      // xcodec + BOTH Vocos decoders are ONE untiered `coRequisite` (componentId `xcodec`) — the
      // approved R2 carve-out: those convnets stay at upstream precision at every tier, and the
      // re-host's `sceneworks-tiers.json` records `tiered: false`. The provider opens exactly three
      // files from the one `xcodec` component directory (`candle_audio_yue::model::XCODEC_COMPONENT_ID`):
      // `final_ckpt/ckpt_00360000.safetensors` (codec encode + decode AND the HuBERT semantic branch,
      // read from its `semantic_model.*` tensors) and the two `decoders/decoder_*.safetensors` Vocos
      // upsamplers. The re-host's `semantic_ckpts/`, `mm_tokenizer_v0.2_hf/` (the mm tokenizer is read
      // from each stage-1 tier dir) and `config.yaml` files are never opened, so they are not
      // downloaded. Its descriptor's `required_components` is
      // exactly `["stage2", "xcodec"]`, which is what these two componentIds provision. Both
      // co-requisites are shared by all six entries (same repo + revision ⇒ one cached snapshot).
      //
      // `files` name every file the loader opens (never `[]`), so a partial snapshot cannot read as
      // installed. Sizes are the per-tier sums from the HF tree API at each pinned revision. Every
      // repo is a SceneWorks safetensors re-host of the Apache-2.0 upstream carrying its LICENSE +
      // NOTICE (About → Licenses: `yue`, `xcodec-mini-infer`).
